From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:27:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Input: ft3658 - make the SPI buffers DMA-safe

SPI transfer buffers must be DMA-safe (include/linux/spi/spi.h,
Documentation/spi/spi-summary.rst), and tx and rx sit in struct ft3658
next to other fields, so a controller with a DMA channel would map
memory those fields share. Put each buffer on its own ARCH_DMA_MINALIGN
boundary, after every other field. On gs201 the USI SPI has no DMA
channel and runs in polling mode, so this changes nothing on the
Pixel 7.

Tested on a Pixel 7 (7.3.0-rc6) with the touch node: the controller
probes (chip id 0x56, firmware 0x16) and reports touches across the
panel with no CRC errors.

Suggested-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c
index d16c4bc09..61fc50514 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/focaltech_ft3658.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
  *	event (2 bits) | x (12) | id (4) | y (12) | pressure | area
  */
 
+#include <linux/cache.h>
 #include <linux/crc-ccitt.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
@@ -77,9 +78,10 @@ struct ft3658 {
 	struct regulator *vdd;
 	struct regulator *avdd;
 	struct touchscreen_properties prop;
-	u8 tx[FT3658_BUF_LEN];
-	u8 rx[FT3658_BUF_LEN];
 	u8 report[FT3658_REPORT_LEN];
+	/* SPI buffers, DMA-safe: each on its own DMA alignment boundary */
+	u8 tx[FT3658_BUF_LEN] __aligned(ARCH_DMA_MINALIGN);
+	u8 rx[FT3658_BUF_LEN] __aligned(ARCH_DMA_MINALIGN);
 };
 
 static int ft3658_read(struct ft3658 *ts, u8 addr, u8 *data, size_t len)
